        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "Implementation: Needs design/spec work. Key decisions: (1) Lifecycle — kspec worktree create @task creates worktree on new branch, kspec worktree cleanup removes it. (2) Shadow branch — worktrees share the same .kspec/ (single source of truth for tasks), or each gets a read-only copy. Sharing is simpler but risks concurrent writes. (3) Naming — branch: agent/<task-slug>, worktree dir: .worktrees/<task-slug>. (4) Integration — ralph could auto-create worktree per task, merge back on completion. Start with manual create/cleanup, add ralph integration later.",
