  {
    "_ulid": "01KHY9XF0Y160G7K8F4K0YVFM4",
    "slugs": [],
    "title": "Spike: Audit mock completeness vs real adapter behavior",
    "type": "spike",
    "description": "The ACP test mock (tests/mocks/acp-mock.js) is minimal and may not reflect real adapter behavior after the upgrade. Needs assessment.\n\n## Current mock limitations\n\n1. Only emits agent_message_chunk — never sends tool_call, tool_call_update, agent_thought_chunk events\n2. No empty-string finalization signal (real Claude Code sends content.text === \"\" to signal stream end)\n3. Permission handling only tested indirectly via mock's mirrored logic\n4. No _meta.claudeCode.* fields in emitted events (tool name/output extraction untested at integration level)\n5. SessionUpdate discriminator values hardcoded as strings, not validated against SDK types\n\n## What to investigate\n\n1. Run a real ralph session and capture events.jsonl\n2. Compare the real SessionUpdate structures against what the mock emits\n3. Identify gaps: which real event patterns are NOT covered by mock or unit tests?\n4. Specifically check:\n   - tool_call events: do they have _meta.claudeCode.toolName in the real adapter?\n   - tool_call_update events: do they have rawOutput or _meta.claudeCode.toolResponse?\n   - Does the real adapter send duplicate tool_call events (the \"alreadyCached\" pattern from PR #316)?\n   - Are there new SessionUpdate variants (e.g. usage_update) that the translator should handle?\n\n## Outcome\n\nEither:\n- The mock is sufficient and unit tests in ralph.test.ts cover the gaps (likely)\n- Or create tasks to extend the mock and/or add integration test scenarios\n\n## Note\n\nThis can be combined with the runtime compatibility spike if convenient — both require running a real ralph session. But the focus here is on test coverage, not adapter compatibility.",
    "spec_ref": null,
    "meta_ref": null,
    "plan_ref": null,
    "status": "pending",
    "blocked_by": [],
    "depends_on": [
      "@01KHY9WV"
    ],
    "context": [],
    "priority": 3,
    "tags": [
      "acp-migration"
    ],
    "vcs_refs": [],
    "created_at": "2026-02-20T19:55:03.581Z",
    "notes": [
      {
        "_ulid": "01KHYA7WMBVHKDE0B37TFY3ASQ",
        "created_at": "2026-02-20T20:00:45.195Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "Automation status set to manual_only: Spikes require interactive runtime testing and human judgment on outcomes",
        "supersedes": null
      },
      {
        "_ulid": "01KHYAGR411TWQZ1GHM6WZF46N",
        "created_at": "2026-02-20T20:05:35.489Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "From changelog review — the mock should be tested against these real adapter behaviors:\n\n1. rawOutput field on tool_call_update events (added v0.14.0)\n2. config_option_update SessionNotification (v0.18.0) — mock doesn't emit this\n3. current_mode_update SessionNotification (v0.14.0) — mock doesn't emit this\n4. Edit tool results with {type: \"diff\"} content blocks (v0.18.0)\n5. Bash results with {type: \"terminal\"} content blocks when terminal_output capability enabled (v0.18.0)\n6. configOptions array in NewSessionResponse (v0.18.0)\n7. Code fence language changed from sh to console in Bash formatted output (v0.18.0)\n\nPriority items: #1 and #4 affect tool output extraction. #2, #3, #5 are new event types that should be gracefully ignored.",
        "supersedes": null
